Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unmarked Users,

I am using the gmultmix function to estimate abundance of fish from a depletion survey.  I have two primary periods (data from 2010 and 2011) and six sites.  Block nets were used during the survey to meet the closed assumption during the survey and the population is open between the primary periods.  I have tried different values of K ranging from 100 to 1100 and the intercept parameter is highly sensitive to my choice of K.  As I increase K the intercept increases.  However, the parameter estimates for the covariates of abundance do not change when K is above 200.  Does this indicate a problem with my data?  I searched the group posts and there was one reference in a pcount string that suggested setting K to a high enough value that the MLE is not affected.  Is this the same case with the gmultmix function?

Thanks in advance,
Jason Doll

From u4a15de51da4445ae at groups.google.com  Sun Feb 12 15:19:45 2012
From: u4a15de51da4445ae at groups.google.com (Jeffrey Royle)
