Hi Jason,

I would also point out that this model is meant for populations that are open with respect to movement (temporary emigration), not for populations that experience movement and births and deaths as is probably the case with multi-year data. If you use it for the latter case, then the super-population size could be very large indeed, and phi could be very low like Andy said. Have you tried analyzing the data from the 2 years separately? A better approach might be to modify the Dail-Madsen model to handle removal sampling data, but we haven't done that yet.

Richard

