hi Jason,
 in my view, without knowing more about this, the extreme sensitivity to K suggests weak identifiability of the temporary emigration parameter, which is probably manifest as a value of phi near 0, suggesting that N[1] and N[2] are almost independent from year to year.
 This shouldn't affect estimates of the covariate parameters which are identifiable even in the limiting case.

 This is something to be aware of in all of the N-mixture models whether the obs model is binomial or multinomial.

regards
andy

