References: <9QoulVoboLQ.9inaleA3DvUJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/9QoulVoboLQ/m/2LnktxDSooQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi BK,

I suggest that you read the first two papers cited on the help page for pcount. You cannot model abundance using obsCovs, because the model is for closed populations... it assumes that abundance does not change over time. If you want to model temporal variation in abundance, see pcountOpen, and read the corresponding paper (Dail and Madsen 2012).

Best,
Richard

