this makes me think about a paper that I reviewed recently where the authors used an N-mixture type of a model but they actually had N[i,t]  and p constant.  With certain covariate models on E[N[i,t]] then it seems like the parameters are identifiable.  This is related to the recent paper here:
@article{sólymos2012conditional,
 title={Conditional likelihood approach for analyzing single visit abundance survey data in the presence of zero inflation and detection error},
 author={S{\'o}lymos, P. and Lele, S. and Bayne, E.},
 journal={Environmetrics},
 year={2012},
 publisher={Wiley Online Library}
}

regards
andy

